# This is an example of how to do pre-repo .envrc files when using the common
# top-level one from one directory up.

# This file is sourced from a top-level .envrc that gets copied to all
# repositories. This file holds repo-specific details while the top-level file
# holds anything common to all repositories. Shellcheck needs to be told it can
# source the top-level file to get at variable definitions, but if we source it
# for real we end up failing because this path won't exist. So wrap this up in
# a never-true conditional so Shellcheck can get at it but real-world usage
# never will.
if false; then
	source  ../envrc
fi

# We need to reload whenever foo changes, because baz is at the bar
watch_file foo
